## Logged Issues

### [Login Page] – [CEO View] – Hardcoded Inline Styles Overriding Theme
Category: 2.1 Visual & design consistency
Repro steps: 
1. Open `/login`.
2. Inspect the `LoginForm` and `page.tsx` wrapper.
Expected: Styles should use Tailwind classes or CSS variables for dark mode compatibility (e.g., `bg-background`, `text-foreground`).
Actual: Extensive use of inline styles (`style={{ background: "#fff", color: "#0f1420" }}`) hardcodes a light-mode appearance.
Fix applied: (To be applied by Dev team) Convert inline styles to Tailwind CSS classes.
Re-tested: N/A

### [LoginForm] – [CEO View] – Insecure Client-Side Token Read
Category: 2.3 Navigation & routing integrity (Security)
Repro steps: 
1. Open `src/components/auth/login-form.tsx`.
2. Observe the `useEffect` checking `document.cookie.match(...)` for a `token`.
Expected: If the token is HttpOnly (as mandated by backend security rules), `document.cookie` will not be able to read it. Client-side should rely on an `/api/auth/me` endpoint or server component passing state.
Actual: The frontend assumes `token` is accessible via `document.cookie`, which breaks redirect logic if security rules are correctly applied on the backend.
Fix applied: (To be applied by Dev team) Remove client-side token read; use a dedicated session check or Next.js middleware.
Re-tested: N/A

### [DashboardClient] – [CEO View] – Export Report Button Misses Blob Parsing
Category: 2.8 Console & network health
Repro steps: 
1. Open `/executive/dashboard`.
2. Click "Export report" button.
Expected: The API response should be validated to ensure it's a valid CSV/Excel blob, and errors should surface clearly if the backend fails.
Actual: The frontend blindly creates a blob from `res.blob()` even if the backend might return a JSON error structure when failing to generate the report (though it catches HTTP non-ok, a 200 JSON error would break). The filename is hardcoded to `.csv` regardless of actual MIME type.
Fix applied: (To be applied by Dev team) Check `Content-Type` headers before assuming the payload is a CSV blob.
Re-tested: N/A

### [QuickLinks] – [CEO View] – Full Page Reloads Instead of SPA Transitions
Category: 2.7 Performance & 2.3 Navigation
Repro steps: 
1. Open `/executive/dashboard`.
2. Click on any link in the "Quick links" widget (e.g., "Organisation Chart").
Expected: Should navigate instantly using Next.js client-side routing (`<Link href="...">`).
Actual: Uses standard HTML `<a href="...">` tags, causing a full page reload and destroying application state.
Fix applied: (To be applied by Dev team) Replace `<a>` tags with `import Link from 'next/link'` and `<Link>`.
Re-tested: N/A

### [QuickLinks] – [CEO View] – Unauthorized Route Link Displayed
Category: 2.9 Consistency within the CEO view
Repro steps: 
1. Open `/executive/dashboard`.
2. Look at the "Quick links" widget.
3. Observe "Audit logs" link pointing to `/admin/audit`.
Expected: Based on the RBAC Permission Matrix, the CEO has no access ("—") to the Audit Log. This link should not be visible to the CEO.
Actual: The UI affords an action the CEO shouldn't have, leading to a likely 403 Forbidden error if clicked.
Fix applied: (To be applied by Dev team) Remove the "Audit logs" link from the CEO dashboard's QuickLinks configuration.
Re-tested: N/A

### [LeavesSummaryWidget] – [CEO View] – Unsafe Type Casting Leading to Potential Crashes
Category: 2.4 Component states
Repro steps: 
1. Load `/executive/dashboard` with a malformed API response for `ceo-leaves-calendar`.
2. Observe the React query hook `data` state.
Expected: The `useMemo` aggregating leave stats should defensively check if `data` is an array.
Actual: It casts `(data as any[]).forEach(...)`. If the API returns an object or null but doesn't trigger a hard HTTP error, the frontend will crash with `data.forEach is not a function`.
Fix applied: (To be applied by Dev team) Add `if (!Array.isArray(data)) return { ... }` inside the `useMemo`.
Re-tested: N/A

